<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import LoopStages from './lib/LoopStages.abide'
import loopStages from './lib/LoopStages.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import PlayStages from './lib/PlayStages.abide'
import playStages from './lib/PlayStages.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import RestOnStage from './lib/RestOnStage.abide'
import restOnStage from './lib/RestOnStage.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import StepMonths from './lib/StepMonths.abide'
import stepMonths from './lib/StepMonths.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import StepStages from './lib/StepStages.abide'
import stepStages from './lib/StepStages.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/tabs', '/headless/virtual-list', '/behaviors/observe']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageCarousel.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("the stages rest on the deal\'s own, each a slide named for its stage"',
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageCarousel.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("next and previous step through the stages, and reset comes back to the deal\'s"',
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageCarousel.test.ts',
            from: ["test('moving the deal to a stage rests the carousel on it'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/ContractViewer.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the arrows go from the last page to the first, and back'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/carousel.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a carousel that loops steps past each end to the other"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/carousel.test.ts',
            from: ["test(\"align start brings an item's start to the scroller's"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/e2e/carousel.spec.ts',
            from: ["test('a carousel aligned by its start shows three and a tenth"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/pipeline/lib/StageTour.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the tour arrives playing, and its button pauses and plays it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/carousel.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('playing steps on its own every autoplay, counted afresh after a step by hand",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/e2e/carousel.spec.ts',
            from: [
                "test('an autoplaying carousel steps by itself, and holds still under the pointer",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/e2e/carousel.spec.ts',
            from: ["test('reduced motion arrives paused, and play starts it"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/carousel.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('what a scroll to an item passes on the way is not current",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/carousel.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('once the scroller reports a snap, the snap target alone sets current",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/e2e/carousel.spec.ts',
            from: ["test('a scroll moves current to the item it snaps to"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Rest a row of stages on the deal's own">
        <p>Spread <code>host</code> on the scroller and <code>item</code> on each stage. The
            page arrives scrolled to the stage <code>selected</code> names, and
            <code>current</code> follows the stage a swipe lands on. The snapping is your CSS:
            give the scroller <code>snap-x</code> and each item <code>snap-center</code>, pad the
            scroller where its neighbours peek (<code>px-[12.5%]</code>) and fill what the padding
            leaves with each item (<code>basis-full</code>), so the first and last stages can
            reach the center too. A percent basis is of the space inside the padding, so
            <code>basis-3/4</code> there would leave the last stage short of it.</p>
        <Example code={restOnStage}><RestOnStage /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Step through stages with buttons, and go back to where it rests">
        <p>Spread <code>previous</code> and <code>next</code> on two buttons: each steps from
            the current stage and is disabled at its end. <code>reset</code> scrolls back to
            the stage the carousel rests on, the first where nothing is selected.</p>
        <Example code={stepStages}><StepStages /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Loop from the last stage back to the first">
        <p>Pass <code>loop: true</code> and <code>next</code> at the last stage goes to the
            first, <code>previous</code> at the first to the last, and neither is disabled. A
            lightbox takes the same option.</p>
        <Example code={loopStages}><LoopStages /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show three and a bit, a month at a time">
        <p>Pass <code>align: 'start'</code> and the carousel lines each item's start up with
            the scroller's, as <code>snap-start</code> does, rather than its center. Make each
            item a little less than a third of the row (<code>basis-[calc(100%/3.1)]</code>)
            and three months show with a sliver of the fourth, and <code>next</code> moves one.
            Near the end, where the row runs out before a month can reach the start,
            <code>next</code> is disabled rather than pressing to no effect.</p>
        <Example code={stepMonths}><StepMonths /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Play through the stages on their own">
        <p>Pass <code>autoplay</code>, the milliseconds between steps, and the carousel steps
            as <code>next</code> does, stopping at the last stage unless it loops. Spread
            <code>play</code> on a button to pause and play it: a carousel that moves on its own
            needs one. It holds still while the pointer is over it or focus is inside it,
            arrives paused for a reader who prefers reduced motion, and tells a screen reader
            nothing while it turns.</p>
        <Example code={playStages}><PlayStages /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
